            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0611" n="539" xml:id="pg539"/>

                <head>No. 337.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 29, 1882</date>.
                        (Received September 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 542.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send herewith, as
                    accompaniments, two copies of the Gaceta Oficial, of July 19, 1882, containing a
                    decree of the President, of date September 3, 1881, and a programme for the
                    celebration of the 24th day of July, 1883—the centennial birthday of Bolivar.
                    The decree indicates that all the Spanish-American republics, the Republic of
                    the United States, the French Republic, the Swiss Confederation, Great Britain,
                    and other nations, will be invited to take part in the celebration. Among
                    various other acts of the proposed procedure, I will note that the 31st day of
                    July is set apart—as I translate from the programme—for: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The inauguration of a monumental statue to George Washington, the father
                            of the great people who founded in the New World the republic which is
                            the model of the Spanish-American nations.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Here is certainly a fine recognition of our Washington and our country.</p>
                <p>When the matter shall be brought to my attention by the minister of exterior
                    relations I will communicate further in the premises.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
